    "result_text": "I added `_allow_redirect` to `hc/accounts/views.py`, just after `POST_LOGIN_ROUTES`. I haven't run the test suite.\n\n`views.py` already called `_allow_redirect` in four places, but nothing defined it, so those calls would have raised `NameError`. The four places are `login`, `_redirect_after_login`, `_check_2fa` and `login_webauthn`. Defining the function fixes all of them without any edit to the login view. The email-link branch of `login` already passes `?next=` through it.\n\nThe function comes from the catalog pattern `accounts.allow_redirect@v1`. It rejects empty values and any URL with a host. It then resolves the path and allows it only if the route name is in `POST_LOGIN_ROUTES`. The pattern's `# pcat:` marker comment is kept above it.\n\n`check_code` reports no deviations from the pattern. An earlier run flagged four high-severity issues, but that was because I had pasted the function without its imports. With the imports and constant included, the report was clean."
